From 85344ea3d6305c3727cfa84b4a84882704e3a380 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cowork <cowork@local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 04:29:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Home page: design fixes from the 2026-07-26 critique (batch 1
 + 2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Batch 1 — typography and iconography
* .hero h1 gets text-wrap: balance. At 1024px the headline was orphaning
  "story." onto its own line; it now breaks at the sentence boundary
  ("Find the place." / "Hear the story."). Unchanged at 1280 and 1440,
  where it still sets on one line.
* .btn now sets font-family: var(--font-sans). A <button> does not inherit
  the body font, so the hero CTA was rendering in the UA default (Arial)
  beside its <a> twin. Measured across the home, concierge and location
  pages: every .btn now resolves to the same stack.
* Dropped the leading pin emoji from "Find places near me". It rendered
  pink against the rust fill and was the only emoji in the button row.
* Added U+FE0F to the telephone glyph in the guide card and the mobile
  bottom nav. Without it U+260E defaults to text presentation and rendered
  monochrome next to two colour emoji.
* Replaced the filled active-page pill in the main nav with a single gold
  underline plus bold weight. The header previously carried two competing
  highlight mechanisms — a pine pill on the current page and gold text on
  Concierge. Gold is now the only accent in the header. The distinction is
  still non-colour (weight + underline) and aria-current is untouched.

Batch 2 — the stat row
* Rebuilt .trust-line as three real stats with middot separators and one
  consistent treatment: serif numerals at 1.45rem in white, lower-case
  labels in sand. Previously three stats and a feature claim shared one
  undifferentiated row.
* Removed "2 reviewed entries". Two of ninety-five is not a number worth
  advertising; it returns when the rewrite programme has run further.
  Replaced with the category count, which is defensible today.
* "Works offline in the field" moves to its own line below the stats,
  since it is a capability claim and not a measurement.

Also removes the "Start with the trip, not the database" eyebrow from the
hero card, per Charles. This supersedes the contrast fix applied to that
same element earlier today.

Verified: astro build clean; axe-core 4.10 WCAG 2.0/2.1 A+AA returns 0
violations at 1440 and 390; active-nav treatment checked on /map, /about
and /concierge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
